   710 000001EE E8C5010000          <1>         call    getk
   711 000001F3 EBD1                <1>         jmp     kt3
   712                              <1> 
   713                              <1> ; '$' prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: '/' plus a character from
   714                              <1> ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; '/' plus any other character
   715                              <1> ; clears that character's bit 6 (/M is CR, /? is DEL's '?'; '/' and '"'
   716                              <1> ; have no bit 6, so // and /" give themselves). EBX itself steps along the
   717                              <1> ; string. It is the last handler: it runs on past the window.
   718                              <1> %if CHECKED
   719                              <1> ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the report's
